<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- RSW_DonorPack_Sarlacc.xml - SWAC PHASE 0 (design/RimMandrake/biome_sprint_kickoff_2026-10-15.md 0.5.2),
     Transient/phase0_p1_questions.md Q1. Owner, 2026-10-15, by question card ("What should happen to the donor's Sarlacc
     landmarks" -> "Port both landmarks").

     Both Sarlacc landmarks of Star Wars Animal Collection (mlie, SW_Buildings_Natural.xml + RulePacks_Namers_Landmarks.xml)
     ported as our own RSW_ defs, so the donor can retire. Every class is vanilla except one genstep (below).
       live pit:  RSW_Sarlacc (LandmarkDef) -> RSW_SarlaccLair (TileMutatorDef) -> RSW_GenStep_SarlaccPit -> one of
                  RSW_SarlaccPit (9x6, the moderate pit) / RSW_SarlaccPitGreat (15x10) / RSW_SarlaccPitColossal (25x17)
                  (corpse-dump work tables; RSW_FeedCorpseToSarlacc / RSW_DoBillsFeedSarlacc)
       dead cave: RSW_DeadSarlacc (LandmarkDef) -> RSW_DeadSarlaccCave (TileMutatorDef) -> RSW_GenStep_DeadSarlaccPit
                  -> RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk (12x9 MapPortal) -> RSW_SarlaccCavity (pocket MapGeneratorDef, exit CaveExit)
     Old -> new names (the canonical save holds the two LandmarkDefs): Transient/phase0_sarlacc_save_renames.md.

     Deliberate differences from the donor:
     - RSW_SarlaccPit keeps the donor's (9,6) footprint EXACTLY: StructureInjectionsSW's sarlacc_ring template is measured
       against it (RSW_GenStep_SarlaccRing anchors on this def, and only this def: its 15x12 clear would cut into a bigger pit,
       so a map that rolled a bigger pit has no ring, skipped quietly by anchorOptional).
     - SARLACC_PIT_WIDEN_THE_BIG_ONES (owner, 2026-10-16, of the accepted 9x6 art: "Superb though that is just a moderate one.
       They can get much bigger."): two bigger sizes on the same art, RSW_SarlaccPitGreat and RSW_SarlaccPitColossal. The
       genstep is RimMandrake.StarWars.SWBestiary.RSW_GenStep_SarlaccPitSized (BeastMechanics assembly): it rolls one size per
       map by weight, falls back to each smaller size when the rolled one finds no room, and lands only the moderate pit when
       the Mod Setting "Great and colossal sarlacc pits" is off. Every size's interactionCellOffset is the first row south of
       its footprint: z = -((sizeZ - 1) / 2) - 1 (RSW_SarlaccPitKernel.InteractionOffsetZ; selftest_sarlacc_pit_sizes.py).
     - The building ThingDef is RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk, not a second "RSW_DeadSarlacc", so a save grep never confuses the
       building with the LandmarkDef.
     - RSW_SarlaccCavity drops the donor's UndercaveMapComponent: that component looks for a PitGate on the source map and,
       finding none, logged a warning on every generation and did nothing else but ambient dust. It also drops the donor's
       Name="Undercave" attribute, which collided with vanilla Anomaly's own abstract name.
     - The donor's wild-plant mutators are dropped from both landmarks' optional mutator chances. Two of them were ported
       2026-10-19 as RSW_WildTattooinePlants / RSW_WildGalacticPlants (RSW_DonorPack_WildPlantMutators.xml); the rest
       were on no tile and are not ported. Every other chance is a vanilla Odyssey/Biotech/Ideology mutator.
     - Odyssey MayRequire guards are dropped: every DLC is assumed and this mod depends on Odyssey.
     ART: no donor pixels. RSW_SarlaccPit, RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk and RSW_SarlacciSpore name OUR texture paths; the renders are
     filed in design/RimMandrake/swac_sarlacc_art_2026-10-15.json (artpipe). Until they install those three defs have no
     texture: do not deploy SWBestiary past this commit before they land. The landmark icons are our own Ash'karr icons
     (AshkarrLandmarkArt), copied here so the defs resolve without that mod. -->
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================= live sarlacc pit ========================= -->

  <!-- Every sarlacc pit size. A child sets defName, label, description, size, graphicData/drawSize, interactionCellOffset,
       Beauty, and its costList / killedLeavings with Inherit="False" (a list would otherwise APPEND to this one). -->
  <ThingDef Name="RSW_SarlaccPitBase" ParentName="BuildingBase" Abstract="True">
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <thingClass>Building_WorkTable</thingClass>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Heavy</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <canOverlapZones>false</canOverlapZones>
    <castEdgeShadows>false</castEdgeShadows>
    <altitudeLayer>FloorEmplacement</altitudeLayer>
    <defaultPlacingRot>South</defaultPlacingRot>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <blockWind>false</blockWind>
    <holdsRoof>false</holdsRoof>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <destroyable>true</destroyable>
    <blockPlants>true</blockPlants>
    <preventSkyfallersLandingOn>true</preventSkyfallersLandingOn>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>true</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <graphicData>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Natural/RSW_SarlaccPit</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <building>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
      <isTargetable>false</isTargetable>
      <isInert>true</isInert>
      <claimable>false</claimable>
      <expandHomeArea>false</expandHomeArea>
      <destroySound>RSW_Pawn_Sarlacc_Wounded</destroySound>
      <spawnedConceptLearnOpportunity>BillsTab</spawnedConceptLearnOpportunity>
    </building>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>1000</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <hasInteractionCell>True</hasInteractionCell>
    <surfaceType>Item</surfaceType>
    <soundImpactDefault>RSW_Pawn_Sarlacc_Death</soundImpactDefault>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap</li>
    </placeWorkers>
    <recipes>
      <li>RSW_FeedCorpseToSarlacc</li>
    </recipes>
    <inspectorTabs>
      <li>ITab_Bills</li>
    </inspectorTabs>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Spawner">
        <thingToSpawn>ChunkSlagSteel</thingToSpawn>
        <spawnCount>1</spawnCount>
        <spawnIntervalRange>300000~600000</spawnIntervalRange>
        <spawnMaxAdjacent>1</spawnMaxAdjacent>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_MeditationFocus">
        <statDef>MeditationFocusStrength</statDef>
        <focusTypes>
          <li>Morbid</li>
        </focusTypes>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_AmbientSound">
        <sound>RSW_Pawn_Sarlacc_Call_Ambient</sound>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_SpawnEffecterOnDestroy">
        <effect>CocoonDestroyed</effect>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>true</drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- The moderate pit: the donor's own size, and the one the accepted art was drawn for. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="RSW_SarlaccPitBase">
    <defName>RSW_SarlaccPit</defName>
    <label>sarlacc pit</label>
    <description>The gaping maw of a juvenile sarlacc creature. The endlessly hungry sarlacc can be used to quickly get rid of various organic corpses and so such sites are popular with various criminal enterprises. It will occasionally regurgitate a small amount of indigestible scrap metal; no doubt leftover from some unlucky "prey".</description>
    <size>(9,6)</size>
    <graphicData>
      <drawSize>(10,10)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-3)</interactionCellOffset>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>-50</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>-50</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>1</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
      <RSW_Silica_Meat>300</RSW_Silica_Meat>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>1</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RSW_SarlaccPitBase">
    <defName>RSW_SarlaccPitGreat</defName>
    <label>great sarlacc pit</label>
    <description>The maw of a mature sarlacc, wide enough to swallow a bantha whole. Its body below the sand is older than any settlement nearby, and it is no less hungry for it: corpses tipped in vanish without a trace, and now and then it coughs up the scrap metal it could not digest.</description>
    <size>(15,10)</size>
    <graphicData>
      <drawSize>(17,17)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-5)</interactionCellOffset>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>-80</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>-80</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>2</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
      <RSW_Silica_Meat>800</RSW_Silica_Meat>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>2</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RSW_SarlaccPitBase">
    <defName>RSW_SarlaccPitColossal</defName>
    <label>colossal sarlacc pit</label>
    <description>The vast maw of an ancient sarlacc, grown over untold centuries into a pit the size of a fortress courtyard. Legends say its prey is digested over a thousand years. Whatever is thrown in is never seen again, save the odd lump of scrap metal it spits back out.</description>
    <size>(25,17)</size>
    <graphicData>
      <drawSize>(28,28)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-9)</interactionCellOffset>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>-120</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>-120</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <costList Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>3</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
      <RSW_Silica_Meat>2000</RSW_Silica_Meat>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings Inherit="False">
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>3</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>RSW_FeedCorpseToSarlacc</defName>
    <label>dump corpse in sarlacc</label>
    <description>Feed a corpse to the sarlacc to completely destroy it.</description>
    <jobString>Dumping corpse.</jobString>
    <workAmount>90</workAmount>
    <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
    <effectWorking>ButcherFlesh</effectWorking>
    <soundWorking>RSW_Pawn_Sarlacc_Butchered</soundWorking>
    <autoStripCorpses>false</autoStripCorpses>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <categories>
            <li>Corpses</li>
          </categories>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <categories>
        <li>Corpses</li>
      </categories>
      <disallowedCategories>
        <li>CorpsesMechanoid</li>
        <li>CorpsesDrone</li>
      </disallowedCategories>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
    <defaultIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>Corpse_Human</li>
      </thingDefs>
      <specialFiltersToAllow>
        <li>AllowCorpsesColonist</li>
        <li>AllowCorpsesSlave</li>
        <li>AllowCorpsesStranger</li>
      </specialFiltersToAllow>
    </defaultIngredientFilter>
  </RecipeDef>

  <WorkGiverDef>
    <defName>RSW_DoBillsFeedSarlacc</defName>
    <label>dumping corpse</label>
    <giverClass>WorkGiver_DoBill</giverClass>
    <workType>Hauling</workType>
    <priorityInType>40</priorityInType>
    <fixedBillGiverDefs>
      <li>RSW_SarlaccPit</li>
    </fixedBillGiverDefs>
    <verb>dump corpse at</verb>
    <gerund>dumping at</gerund>
    <requiredCapacities>
      <li>Manipulation</li>
    </requiredCapacities>
    <prioritizeSustains>true</prioritizeSustains>
  </WorkGiverDef>

  <TileMutatorDef>
    <defName>RSW_SarlaccLair</defName>
    <label>sarlacc pit</label>
    <description>This area hosts a juvenile sarlacc creature. These sessile creatures are known to have millennia-long lifespans; the circular maws on the surface are supported by a massive underground body.</description>
    <biomeBlacklist>
      <li>SeaIce</li>
      <li>IceSheet</li>
      <li>GlacialPlain</li>
    </biomeBlacklist>
    <maxHilliness>Mountainous</maxHilliness>
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>RSW_GenStep_SarlaccPit</li>
    </extraGenSteps>
  </TileMutatorDef>

  <!-- order=950 is load-bearing: RSW_GenStep_SarlaccRing (StructureInjectionsSW, order 960) anchors on the pit this lands. -->
  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RSW_GenStep_SarlaccPit</defName>
    <order>950</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.SWBestiary.RSW_GenStep_SarlaccPitSized">
      <thingDef>RSW_SarlaccPit</thingDef>
      <!-- smallest first: the first is what the setting's off state and every fallback ends on -->
      <sizes>
        <li><thingDef>RSW_SarlaccPit</thingDef><weight>0.5</weight><clearSpaceSize>10</clearSpaceSize></li>
        <li><thingDef>RSW_SarlaccPitGreat</thingDef><weight>0.35</weight><clearSpaceSize>16</clearSpaceSize></li>
        <li><thingDef>RSW_SarlaccPitColossal</thingDef><weight>0.15</weight><clearSpaceSize>26</clearSpaceSize></li>
      </sizes>
      <createUsedRect>true</createUsedRect>
      <allowInWaterBiome>false</allowInWaterBiome>
      <skipRoofed>true</skipRoofed>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>1~1</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <clearSpaceSize>10</clearSpaceSize>
      <terrainValidationDisallowed>
        <li>Road</li>
      </terrainValidationDisallowed>
      <count>1</count>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

  <RulePackDef>
    <defName>RSW_NamerLandmark_Sarlacc</defName>
    <include>
      <li>WorldFeatureNamerCommon</li>
    </include>
    <rulePack>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>r_name(p=0.3)->Pit of [NamePerson]</li>
        <li>r_name(p=0.2)->The [dread] [terrain_word]</li>
        <li>r_name(p=0.1)->The [terrain_word]</li>
        <li>r_name(p=0.05)->Sarlacc Pit</li>
        <li>terrain_word->sarlacc</li>
        <li>terrain_word->sarlacci burrow</li>
        <li>terrain_word->creature</li>
        <li>dread->dreaded</li>
        <li>dread->grim</li>
        <li>dread->vile</li>
        <li>dread->dark</li>
        <li>dread->great</li>
        <li>dread->mighty</li>
        <li>dread->eternal</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </rulePack>
  </RulePackDef>

  <LandmarkDef>
    <defName>RSW_Sarlacc</defName>
    <label>sarlacc pit</label>
    <iconTexturePath>World/Landmarks/RSW_Sarlacc</iconTexturePath>
    <atlasSize>(2, 2)</atlasSize>
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <nameMaker>RSW_NamerLandmark_Sarlacc</nameMaker>
    <mutatorChances>
      <RSW_SarlaccLair Required="True" />
      <Pollution_Increased>0.02</Pollution_Increased>
      <Junkyard>0.05</Junkyard>
      <ArcheanTrees>0.01</ArcheanTrees>
      <MineralRich>0.05</MineralRich>
      <AncientUplink>0.02</AncientUplink>
      <Stockpile>0.05</Stockpile>
      <AnimalLife_Decreased>0.15</AnimalLife_Decreased>
      <Sandy>0.05</Sandy>
      <DryGround>0.05</DryGround>
      <InsectMegahive>0.02</InsectMegahive>
      <FoggyMutator>0.05</FoggyMutator>
    </mutatorChances>
    <comboLandmarkMutators>
      <Dunes>0.05</Dunes>
      <Sandy>0.02</Sandy>
      <Hollow>0.02</Hollow>
      <Chasm>0.02</Chasm>
      <Valley>0.01</Valley>
      <Cavern>0.01</Cavern>
    </comboLandmarkMutators>
  </LandmarkDef>

  <!-- ========================= dead sarlacc cave ========================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk</defName>
    <label>dead sarlacc</label>
    <description>The remnant of a dead sarlacc creature. Perhaps disease, starvation, predation from burrowing insects or maybe even old age has killed it, leaving behind a cavern that its body once filled.</description>
    <size>(12,9)</size>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <thingClass>MapPortal</thingClass>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Heavy</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <canOverlapZones>false</canOverlapZones>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Natural/RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(15,15)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>FloorEmplacement</altitudeLayer>
    <fillPercent>0</fillPercent>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <holdsRoof>true</holdsRoof>
    <destroyable>true</destroyable>
    <preventSkyfallersLandingOn>true</preventSkyfallersLandingOn>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>true</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <building>
      <isEdifice>true</isEdifice>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
      <isTargetable>false</isTargetable>
      <isInert>true</isInert>
      <claimable>false</claimable>
      <expandHomeArea>false</expandHomeArea>
    </building>
    <portal>
      <pocketMapGenerator>RSW_SarlaccCavity</pocketMapGenerator>
      <exitDef>CaveExit</exitDef>
      <enteredLetterLabel>Sarlacc grave</enteredLetterLabel>
      <enteredLetterText>In the depths of a dead sarlacc. Not much here but rocks and rubble and dead flesh. Quite the morbid tourist attraction!</enteredLetterText>
      <enteredLetterDef>PositiveEvent</enteredLetterDef>
    </portal>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>1000</MaxHitPoints>
      <Beauty>-50</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>-50</BeautyOutdoors>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <inspectorTabs>
      <li>ITab_ContentsMapPortal</li>
    </inspectorTabs>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Sealable">
        <sealTexPath>UI/Commands/FillInCaveEntrance</sealTexPath>
        <sealCommandLabel>Collapse sarlacc cavity</sealCommandLabel>
        <sealCommandDesc>Choose a colonist to permanently collapse the sarlacc cavity entrance. Anything or anyone left below will be lost forever.</sealCommandDesc>
        <cannotSealLabel>Cannot collapse</cannotSealLabel>
        <confirmSealText>Collapsing the sarlacc cavity is permanent. Anything or anyone left below will be lost forever.{0}\n\nAre you sure you want to continue?</confirmSealText>
        <destroyPortal>true</destroyPortal>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_LeaveFilthOnDestroyed">
        <filthDef>Filth_Slime</filthDef>
        <thickness>2</thickness>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <costList>
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>1</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
    </costList>
    <killedLeavings>
      <RSW_SarlacciSpore>1</RSW_SarlacciSpore>
    </killedLeavings>
  </ThingDef>

  <MapGeneratorDef>
    <defName>RSW_SarlaccCavity</defName>
    <label>sarlacc cavity</label>
    <isUnderground>true</isUnderground>
    <forceCaves>true</forceCaves>
    <ignoreAreaRevealedLetter>true</ignoreAreaRevealedLetter>
    <disableCallAid>true</disableCallAid>
    <pocketMapProperties>
      <biome>Underground</biome>
      <temperature>15</temperature>
      <tileMutators>
        <li>UndergroundCave</li>
      </tileMutators>
    </pocketMapProperties>
    <genSteps>
      <li>ElevationFertility</li>
      <li>MutatorPostElevationFertility</li>
      <li>Underground_RocksFromGrid</li>
      <li>Terrain</li>
      <li>Plants</li>
      <li>MutatorPostTerrain</li>
      <li>MutatorCriticalStructures</li>
      <li>MutatorNonCriticalStructures</li>
      <li>RockChunks</li>
      <li>PlaceCaveExit</li>
      <li>Fleshbulbs</li>
      <li>Fleshmass</li>
      <li>FleshSacks</li>
      <li>MutatorFinal</li>
      <li>Fog</li>
    </genSteps>
  </MapGeneratorDef>

  <TileMutatorDef>
    <defName>RSW_DeadSarlaccCave</defName>
    <label>a dead sarlacc</label>
    <description>This area hosts a dead sarlacc creature. These sessile creatures are known to have millennia-long lifespans, but are ultimately mortal. Whether from disease, starvation, burrowing insectoids or even old age they eventually die and leave a cavern where the bulk of their corpse has rotted away.</description>
    <biomeBlacklist>
      <li>SeaIce</li>
      <li>IceSheet</li>
      <li>GlacialPlain</li>
    </biomeBlacklist>
    <maxHilliness>Mountainous</maxHilliness>
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>RSW_GenStep_DeadSarlaccPit</li>
    </extraGenSteps>
  </TileMutatorDef>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RSW_GenStep_DeadSarlaccPit</defName>
    <order>950</order>
    <genStep Class="GenStep_ScatterThings">
      <thingDef>RSW_DeadSarlaccHusk</thingDef>
      <createUsedRect>true</createUsedRect>
      <allowInWaterBiome>false</allowInWaterBiome>
      <skipRoofed>true</skipRoofed>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>1~1</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <clearSpaceSize>10</clearSpaceSize>
      <terrainValidationDisallowed>
        <li>Road</li>
      </terrainValidationDisallowed>
      <count>1</count>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

  <LandmarkDef>
    <defName>RSW_DeadSarlacc</defName>
    <label>dead sarlacc</label>
    <iconTexturePath>World/Landmarks/RSW_DeadSarlacc</iconTexturePath>
    <atlasSize>(2, 2)</atlasSize>
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <mutatorChances>
      <RSW_DeadSarlaccCave Required="True" />
      <Pollution_Increased>0.02</Pollution_Increased>
      <Junkyard>0.05</Junkyard>
      <ArcheanTrees>0.01</ArcheanTrees>
      <MineralRich>0.05</MineralRich>
      <AncientUplink>0.02</AncientUplink>
      <Stockpile>0.05</Stockpile>
      <AnimalLife_Increased>0.05</AnimalLife_Increased>
      <AnimalHabitat>0.15</AnimalHabitat>
      <PlantLife_Increased>0.03</PlantLife_Increased>
      <Fertile>0.05</Fertile>
      <Sandy>0.05</Sandy>
      <DryGround>0.05</DryGround>
      <InsectMegahive>0.04</InsectMegahive>
      <FoggyMutator>0.05</FoggyMutator>
    </mutatorChances>
    <comboLandmarkMutators>
      <Dunes>0.05</Dunes>
      <Sandy>0.02</Sandy>
      <Hollow>0.02</Hollow>
      <Chasm>0.02</Chasm>
      <Valley>0.01</Valley>
      <Cavern>0.01</Cavern>
    </comboLandmarkMutators>
  </LandmarkDef>

  <!-- ========================= the spore both leave ========================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RSW_SarlacciSpore</defName>
    <label>sarlacci spore</label>
    <description>The spore of a sarlacc creature. It appears dormant and whilst ugly, it is no less valuable as a naturally occurring curiosity.</description>
    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>4.0</Mass>
      <Beauty>-2.0</Beauty>
      <MarketValue>750</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/RSW_SarlacciSpore</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(1.5, 1.5)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
